# Sound cues (Southampton Refine)

Play short audio so the user hears status without reading chat. Same CLI as other projects:

```bash
python3 ~/Projects/agent-soundboard/scripts/play.py <id>
```

In Cursor Shell, use `required_permissions: ["all"]` if audio does not play.

Default: command exits at once; audio continues in background. Do not use `--wait` unless the user asks.

## Core (most sessions)

| id | when |
| --- | --- |
| `done` | Substantive work finished (queue item chunk, script run, docs)—user can return |
| `need-you` | Blocked: `site/LOCK.json`, `human-confirm-fix`, approval, or only the user can act in-game |
| `error` | Unrecoverable failure the user must know (apply broken, cannot proceed safely) |

After `done`, do not write empty closers (“Done”, “All done”)—state what changed or what to verify.

## Optional flair (rare)

Meme-style ids from the shared soundboard. **Sparingly**—not every chat, not small edits. Usually **once** at the end of a **long** arc (full queue item through apply/verify, session handoff, major milestone). **Default stays `done`.** One flair cue max per task. Real accuracy or apply failures → `error`, not trombone.

| id | Southampton-ish when |
| --- | --- |
| `yay` | Long build phase landed cleanly; light celebratory beat |
| `vine-boom` | Big “there it is” moment after heavy kit work or a punchline fix |
| `epic-impact` | Large milestone (place review done, major pass complete) |
| `party-cheer` | Festive win after long grind (not every apply) |
| `whoosh` | Rare punctuation when handing off a big reveal |
| `fail-wah` / `sad-horn` | Long effort fizzled in a **low-stakes** way—never for wrong geometry in the real world |

More detail: `~/Projects/agent-soundboard/sounds/reference/youtube-cliche/SOURCES.md`
